### Version Used

`main` at 9376c7a1aca, through `RazorFormatter.TryFormatAsync` (the `dotnet format` entry point), with the default formatting options and the shared test project's imports. Found while working on #86310.

### Steps to Reproduce

```razor
<div>
<button @onclick="flag
                  ? A
                  : B"
   class="x">y</button>
</div>
@code {
    bool flag;
    void A() { }
    void B() { }
}
```

### Expected Behavior

The `? A` and `: B"` lines move together, by the same 4 columns as the tag.

### Actual Behavior

```razor
<div>
    <button @onclick="flag
                      ? A
                  : B"
        class="x">y</button>
</div>
@code {
    bool flag;
    void A() { }
    void B() { }
}
```

Only the `? A` line moves; `: B"` stays where it was. (`class` lands one level too shallow too, which is #86306, fixed by #86310.)

