### Describe the bug

The command `dotnet list package --format json` generates invalid JSON with non-espaced double quotes in error message when the dotnet restore fails. The "text" property contains non-escaped literal double quotes, so the JSON parsing fails.

### Steps to reproduce

Inside an empty folder, create an empty .csproj file and run the command `dotnet list package --format json`



### Expected behavior

Output message in english:

``{
   "version": 1,
   "problems": [
      {
         "text": "Restore failed. Run `dotnet restore` for more details on the issue.",
         "level": "error"
      }
   ]
}``

Output with PT-BR localized text:

``{
   "version": 1,
   "problems": [
      {
         "text": "Falha na restauração. Execute `dotnet restore` para obter mais detalhes sobre o problema.",
         "level": "error"
      }
   ]
}``

### Actual behavior

Output with PT-BR localized text:

``{
   "version": 1,
   "problems": [
      {
         "text": "Falha na restauração. Execute "dotnet restore" para obter mais detalhes sobre o problema.",
         "level": "error"
      }
   ]
}``

The double quotes instead of backticks around `dotnet restore` are breaking the JSON syntax.

